## Why This Is Asked
This question tests end-to-end understanding of a data freshness workflow using GCP primitives. It validates knowledge of event-driven validation, scheduled checks, observability, and idempotent design patterns—all essential skills for data engineering roles.

## Key Concepts
- **Cloud Functions**: Event-driven validation triggered on bucket uploads
- **Cloud Scheduler**: Periodic triggers for batch freshness computation
- **BigQuery**: Centralized freshness ledger with `insertId`-based deduplication
- **Cloud Monitoring**: Alerting policies to detect data lag
- **IAM Least Privilege**: Minimal role bindings per service account

## Code Example
```javascript
// Validation trigger
exports.validateAndStore = (event, context) => {
  const data = parseEvent(event);
  if (!schemaValid(data)) {
    throw new Error('Schema validation failed');
  }
  return copyToValidated(data, context);
};

// Freshness checker (scheduled)
exports.checkFreshness = async () => {
  const latestDate = await getLatestValidatedDate();
  const recordCount = await countRecords(latestDate);
  const lag = daysBetween(latestDate, new Date());

  await bigquery.insert({
    insertId: formatDate(latestDate),
    latestDate,
    recordCount,
    lag,
    checkedAt: new Date()
  });

  if (lag > 1) {
    console.log(`Alert: Lag is ${lag} days`);
  }
};
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical usage of scheduled exports, storage event triggers, and idempotent processing in a basic backup workflow. It also evaluates IAM scoping and lifecycle management.

## Key Concepts
- Cloud Scheduler for periodic tasks
- Cloud SQL export to Cloud Storage
- Cloud Functions triggered by storage events (objectFinalize)
- Idempotent file naming and conditional processing
- Storage Lifecycle rules for retention

## Code Example
```javascript
// Cloud Function (Node.js) skeleton
const {Storage} = require('@google-cloud/storage');
const storage = new Storage();

exports.backupPostProcess = async (event, context) => {
  const bucketName = event.bucket;
  const srcName = event.name; // e.g., dumps/db-20260113.sql.gz
  const destName = srcName
    .replace('dumps/', 'backups/archived/')
    .replace(/\.gz$/, '.sql.gz');
  const bucket = storage.bucket(bucketName);
  const dest = bucket.file(destName);
  const [exists] = await dest.exists();
  if (exists) return;
  await bucket.file(srcName).copy(dest);
  await bucket.file(srcName).delete();
};
```

